      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q1",
      "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x + 4y - 3 = 0\"></span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = mx + 7\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> are perpendicular,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> meet at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
