      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>A tree was planted in the ground.</p><p>Its height, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> metres, was measured <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years after planting.</p><p>Exactly 3 years after planting, the height of the tree was 2.35 metres.</p><p>Exactly 6 years after planting, the height of the tree was 3.28 metres.</p><p>Using a linear model,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) find an equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The height of the tree was approximately 140 cm when it was planted.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Explain whether or not this fact supports the use of the linear model in part (a).</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
