    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q7",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{k^2}{x} + 1 \\quad x \\in \\mathbb{R}, x \\neq 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> stating the equation of the horizontal asymptote.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = -2x + 5\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of any point of intersection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is given by a solution of the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^2 - 4x + k^2 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Hence find the exact values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is a tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
