    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q11",
      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x) = 2x^3 - 13x^2 + 8x + 48\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x - 4)\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence, using algebra, show that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x) = 0\"></span> has only two distinct roots.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:112mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Graph of the cubic f.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x)\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Deduce, giving reasons for your answer, the number of real roots of the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^3 - 13x^2 + 8x + 46 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant and the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x + k)\"></span> passes through the origin,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) find the two possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
