      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q13",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:90mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q13-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Area R bounded by the cubic curve, the axis and the line x = k.\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = 2x^3 - 17x^2 + 40x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The curve has a minimum turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = k\"></span>.</p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 3, is bounded by the curve, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = k\"></span>.</p><p>Show that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{256}{3}\"></span></p><p>(Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are not acceptable.)</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p>",
