      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2019-june/q16",
      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) Two non-zero vectors, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf b\"></span>, are such that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|\\mathbf a + \\mathbf b| = |\\mathbf a| + |\\mathbf b|\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Explain, geometrically, the significance of this statement.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) Two different vectors, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf m\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf n\"></span>, are such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\mathbf m| = 3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\mathbf m - \\mathbf n| = 6\"></span>. The angle between vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf m\"></span> and vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf n\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\"></span>.</p><p>Find the angle between vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf m\"></span> and vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf m - \\mathbf n\"></span>, giving your answer, in degrees, to one decimal place.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
